I made four commits beyond the merges, all small and easy to revert:
- **REDO-safe baseline** (`24c8e539`): I added two renamed lines to the REDO-safe review list. The compiler renumbered `StartCdEditAsync` from d__40 to d__41 after #1923, and #1970 moved the level write into `TryStorePipeInverts`. This is a REDO-safety call made by Sonnet, so **the Opus finalizer must confirm it**. If it disagrees, revert that commit and the guard goes red.
- **C-79a test** (`2363cc1a`): the C-79a test saying the #1923 switch is absent now says it is absent or ships OFF.
- **Source-shape pins** (`f5eebc77`): two tests pinned the exact code of #1952 and #1950, which those PRs changed on purpose. I updated them and kept their intent; the #1952 pin now also checks the reader is still an open-close read.
- **Switch tests** (`4445c243`): the new `C79b1NewSwitchDefaultsTests` class above.

